0 !FORAGE {"id":"ACH-Z06-S01","type":"scene","zone":"Z06","lines":"18.590–608","pieces":321,"subBuilds":21,"depth":2,"joints":1397,"anchored":127,"held":194,"detached":0,"studs":[192,174],"height":{"ldu":1175,"bricks":49,"plates":147},"cm":[153.6,139.2,47],"metals":{"gold":84,"silver":25,"bronze":70,"tin":69,"kyanos":40,"niello":8,"crimson":22,"flora":3},"status":"GREEN"}
0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z06-S01","name":"Zone VI · Scene 1: The Daedalean Choros Dance & The River Oceanus Rim","zone":"Z06","lines":"18.590–608","greek":"Ἐν δὲ χορὸν ποίκιλλε περικλυτὸς Ἀμφιγυήεις, τῷ ἴκελον οἷόν ποτ᾽ ἐνὶ Κνωσῷ εὐρείῃ Δαίδαλος ἤσκησεν καλλιπλοκάμῳ Ἀριάδνῃ. ἔνθα μὲν ἠΐθεοι καὶ παρθένοι ἀλφεσίβοιαι ὠρχεῦντ᾽, ἀλλήλων ἐπὶ καρπῷ χεῖρας ἔχοντες... ὡς ὅτε τις τροχὸν ἄρμενον ἐν παλάμῃσιν ἑζόμενος κεραμεὺς πειρήσεται, αἴ κε θέῃσιν· ἄλλοτε δ᾽ αὖ θρέξασκον ἐπὶ στίχας ἀλλήλοισι... ἐν δ᾽ ἐτίθει ποταμοῖο μέγα σθένος Ὠκεανοῖο ἄντυγα πὰρ πυμάτην σάκεος πύκα ποιητοῖο.","buckley":"On it also the illustrious Vulcan embellished a dance, like unto that which in wide Gnossus Daedalus once composed for fair-haired Ariadne. There the youths and the alluring virgins danced, having their hands on each other’s wrists... At one time they would move very lightly with skilled feet, as when a potter sitting shall make trial of a wheel fitted to his hands, whether it will run; and at another time they would move in series towards each other. A large crowd stood around the enjoyable dance, delighted; and among them two tumblers, beginning their song, spun round in the midst. But in it he placed the vast strength of the river Oceanus, around the extreme border of the well-formed shield.","worldModel":{"vision":"Labyrinthine Knossian mosaic pavement in white, gold, and kyanos; maidens in garlands and youths with golden daggers on silver belts; two central tumblers; and the outer ring of River Oceanus.","memory":"Bimodal choreographic state machine: Mode A = circular rotation like a potter’s trial wheel (τροχός); Mode B = linear counter-marching rows (ἐπὶ στίχας); bounded externally by the continuous circular current of Oceanus.","controller":"Artifice mirroring artifice: Daedalus’s Knossian choros and the potter’s wheel inside Hephaestus’s shield, closed by the cosmic river."}}

